  "body": "Stacked on #961 (branch `issue/869-coolant-air`; this PR's own change is the top commit, 5d8b71e2). Fork synced at v0.18.0.\n\n## What changed\nA touch probe section (a section that states a speed of 0, the #523 / #574 test) now starts no coolant on any shipped mill post - no M7 / M8 / M88 at its start, so no M9 / M89 for it at its end - whatever the op's coolant ask and whether or not the machine states coolant codes.\n\n- `fanuc`, `haas`, `sinumerik`, `heidenhain`, `mazak`: `coolant = probeStop ? \"\" : coolantFor(coolantAsk);` (reusing the existing #574 `probeStop`).\n- `doosan-dnm`: same gate on a new `touchProbe` (this post posted M8 for a probe even with no machine).\n- `carvera`: same gate (it posts no probing, but the law holds).\n- `tormach`: already gated (#108 / #362), unchanged.\n\nFixed in the posts, not the stream: `post::dump` does not know a section is a probe, the TOUCH / FOUND records arrive after the preamble, `tormach.cps` reads no `PARAM Coolant` (a stream-side `Coolant off` would be refused there), and a recorded probe stream with no `PARAM Coolant` would still post flood. An explicit Mist / Air / Through-tool ask on a probe op is neither posted nor refused. Why, and what was dropped: `docs/decisions/995-probe-no-coolant.md`.\n\n## How tested\n- New `crates/app/tests/probe_no_coolant.rs` (5 tests, every mill post): `a_probe_section_starts_no_coolant_on_a_machine_that_states_coolants`, `a_probe_section_starts_no_coolant_without_a_machine`, `a_probe_section_ignores_an_explicit_coolant_ask`, `a_bore_centre_probe_posts_no_coolant_on_doosan_dnm` (the issue's TOUCH-record probe stream, with and without `doosan-dnm.mch`), and the control `a_cutting_section_still_starts_its_coolant`. 4 of the 5 fail on #961's posts, the control passes on both.\n- `cargo xtask gate quick --base origin/issue/869-coolant-air`: green. Since `.cps` changes are not gate-mapped, 47 app suites touching posts / probing / coolant were run by hand (fanuc_post, conformance, carvera_post, doosan_dnm_post, probe_op, probe_dialects, probe_tormach, probe_guard, probe_spindle_stop, coolant, coolant_air, coolant_followups, heidenhain_cycles, inverted_post, inverted_probe, posting, tormach_post, ...): all green. clippy on the new suite: clean.\n- Goldens moved: none. Every committed probe golden is posted machine-less, where only Doosan posted coolant, and Doosan has no committed probe golden.\n\n## Not exercised\n- The #926 per-post `probe` golden of `doosan-dnm` lives in #1002 (unmerged), where it is listed as a known bug; whichever of #1002 / this PR merges second drops that known-bug entry and records the golden without M8 / M9.\n- The lathe posts (they probe nothing) and the plasma post (it refuses coolant outright).\n- Left open: doosan-dnm still writes no M5 ahead of a probe's first move (#574 covered the other mill posts) - filed separately.\n\nChangelog: A touch probe section posts no coolant (no M7 / M8 / M9 for it) on every mill post, with or without a machine stating coolants\n\nEffort: high (no escalation)\n\nFixes #995\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
